/datum/lore/character_background/religion/species/scori/general
	name = "Buried Ones"
	id = "religion_scori_general"
	category = "Scorian"
	desc = "Scorians who feel no particular leaning towards a particular buried one will tend to only invoke whichever one \
	is relevant to their current task or situation. This covers both the not-particularly devout (for a scorian) as well as \
	those who prefer not to show favoritism."

/datum/lore/character_background/religion/species/scori/mother
	name = "Mother"
	id = "religion_scori_mother"
	category = "Scorian"
	desc = "While nearly all scorians acknowledge and will even pray to and give thanks to almost all the buried ones, a henotheistic \
	reverence to Mother in particular is extremely common. Regarded as the personification of Surt itself, it isn't \
	difficult to see why this would be the case. She is seen as a nurturing and protective figure, whose gifts of lead, \
	copper and other minerals are used in many applications. Meanwhile goliaths and gutshanks, whose meat, bones, hides and \
	carapaces are utterly essential to scorian society, are regarded as her children in equal measure to the scorians themselves."

/datum/lore/character_background/religion/species/scori/father
	name = "Father"
	id = "religion_scori_father"
	category = "Scorian"
	desc = "A loose conglomeration of heretical fringe beliefs, some scorians revere the Father who is otherwise shunned \
	by most scorians as an agent of chaos and corruption. Scorians who revere the Father tend to have a more nuanced view \
	of Mother and the other buried ones, seeing both good and bad qualities in many who are commonly seen as entirely benevolent. \
	This also applies to the Father himself, who is sometimes interpreted by those who worship him as something like a trickster deity, \
	testing and pushing scorians into danger for their own edification."
